+// DCS Control (0090): known limits of the cursor's redraw as flown on
+// 2026-11-15 and 16. A comment only, nothing is changed.
+// - A cross arm lying on a bright green line of the HUD is drawn dark or
+//   washed out for one synthetic frame: 3 of 54 synthetic frames with two
+//   layers and 2 of 54 composed, per eye, with 37 to 53 % of the arm's
+//   yellow gone in that frame. The sprite is told from the scene by how
+//   close a pixel's colour is to its own (the test below), and yellow on
+//   bright green fails it. A second criterion would bring its own
+//   look-alikes; none was tried.
+// - Over bright cockpit areas the cursor is redrawn less often, and less
+//   with two layers than composed (237 of 450 pairs against 696 of 900 in
+//   one stretch low in the cockpit). The game draws it soft and fat there,
+//   its match with the template is weak and the pair is refused before
+//   this test is reached ("score too low"). A refused pair shows the
+//   interpolated cursor, a fainter smeared cross, never a cross in a wrong
+//   place.
 float cursor_likeness(float3 colour, float3 reference) {
     float3 chroma = colour / max(colour.r + colour.g + colour.b, 1.0e-4);
     float3 wanted = reference / max(reference.r + reference.g + reference.b, 1.0e-4);
